{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789305827,"nonce":"yBokcFakkpikd45m/dkvrc2YH/k=","title":"The benchmark sweep built HEAD's workspace crates from the base","message":"Since 8becd42 the bench workflow builds the A/B base in a worktree that\nshares target/ with HEAD, and builds it first. HEAD is checked out before\nthat, so every HEAD source file is older than the base's fingerprints, and\ncargo judges a path crate fresh by comparing source mtimes with the\nfingerprint: HEAD's workspace crates were only rebuilt when their unit\nhash changed (features, dependency graph), never because their source\ndid. Path packages hash by their path relative to the workspace root, so\nthe two worktrees share fingerprint directories.\n\nSweep 34759043072 (HEAD 2fc5051, base 4a7f979) failed loudly:\n`cargo build -p ash_std` finished in 0.08s, `air` was not compiled, and\n`ash_core` (rebuilt because its features changed) failed against the\nbase's `air` -- no `inline_sites`, no `Pos { site }`.\n\nEarlier sweeps failed silently, shipping a \"HEAD\" binary with base crates:\n- 34683845184 (HEAD 8becd42, base 51d0b33): std changed, not rebuilt.\n- 34704649768 (HEAD 6edf54a, base 8becd42): air (the widen fixes) and std\n  changed, neither rebuilt; ash_interp was.\n- 34749820530 (HEAD 4a7f979, base 6edf54a): air differed by a lint only;\n  std was rebuilt. Sound.\nThe in-sweep A/B deltas published from the first two are not HEAD vs base\nfor those crates.\n\nReproduced in a two-crate toy workspace: base worktree built into the\nshared target after HEAD's checkout; HEAD's `cargo build` finishes in\n0.00s and the binary is the base's; dirtying only the top crate gives the\nCI error shape; `git ls-files -z | xargs -0 touch` before HEAD's build\nmakes cargo rebuild every workspace crate. The touch lives in HEAD's build\nstep so a base that fails part-way cannot skip it. Registry and git\ndependencies are unaffected either way (their fingerprints are not\nmtime-based), so the shared target still saves their compile.","files":null}]}